# Knowledge Graph

## Directory Layout

```
knowledge-graph/
├── specs/           # Individual spec JSON files
├── edges/           # Relationship definitions
├── templates/       # Spec templates
└── schema/          # JSON schema definitions
```

The `knowledge-graph/` directory is git-backed runtime data. Changes are committed automatically by the application.

## Spec JSON Structure

Each spec is a JSON file with at minimum: `id`, `title`, `content`, `status`, `tags`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`.

## Validation

- All spec JSON must validate against the schema in `knowledge-graph/schema/`.
- Edge references must point to existing spec IDs.
- Tags are lowercase, hyphenated strings.

## Git Conventions for KG Changes

- Automated commits from the app use the format: `kg: {action} {spec-title}` (e.g., `kg: create spec "Auth Flow"`).
- Manual edits to `knowledge-graph/` should use: `kg(manual): description`.

## Sandbox Note

The knowledge graph module in `server/src/modules/knowledge-graph/` handles CRUD operations, validation, and git integration. Changes to the `knowledge-graph/` data directory should always flow through this module — never edit spec files directly from other modules.
